          "role": "assistant",
          "text": "For your 420 sq. ft. backyard office with a 10-inch wall thickness, our computed planning volume is **9.9 cubic metres** of hemp-lime. \n\nRegarding your questions:\n* **Code:** Hemp-lime construction is referenced in Appendix BL of the 2024 International Residential Code, but that model code reference does not guarantee local adoption or permit approval; you will need to check with your local authority having jurisdiction.\n* **Structural loads:** Hempcrete is a non-load-bearing insulation infill and cannot hold up a roof on its own—it requires a structural frame (such as timber framing) to carry all roof, floor, wind, and dead loads.\n* **Timeline:** Finishing the entire build in three weeks is very tight. While cast-in-place forms can often come off the next day, natural curing of the hemp-lime wall before final plastering typically takes 3 to 6 weeks depending on weather conditions (though pre-cast blocks are sometimes chosen for speed). Furthermore, live engineering, formal pricing, permitting approvals, and exact site inventory cannot be determined from product facts alone.\n\nAre you planning to use a timber frame to support the roof load for this backyard office?",
